Problem: dangerouslySetInnerHTML has a regex replace but is incomplete.
Server-side sanitize + add alt fallback snippet (replace in page rendering before dangerouslySetInnerHTML):
const sanitizedContent = (post.content || '')
  .replace(/<img([^>]*?)>/gi, (match, attr) => {
    // if already has alt, keep
    if (/\balt=/.test(attr)) return `<img${attr}>`;
    // extract src
    const srcMatch = /src=\"([^\"]+)\"/.exec(attr) || /src='([^']+)'/.exec(attr);
    const src = srcMatch ? srcMatch[1].split('/').pop().replace(/\W+/g, ' ').replace(/\s+/g, ' ') : '';
    const altText = src ? src : post.title;
    return `<img${attr} alt="${altText}" />`;
  });
Then use dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: sanitizedContent }}.

